      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Firebase Admin**\n\nI've decided to use Firebase Authentication for managing user accounts in the `register_user.py` file. Specifically, I'll leverage the Firebase Admin SDK to handle the registration process. This provides a robust and recognizable solution for authentication.\n\n\n**Implementing Registration with Firebase**\n\nI'm now implementing user registration within `register_user.py` using the Firebase Admin SDK. The goal is to establish user accounts with email and password credentials. I've decided to employ Firebase Authentication for robust account management. I am including Firebase-specific code to make its use apparent. Next, I'll focus on initializing the SDK, assuming the service account key path will be provided, perhaps as an environment variable, and will proceed accordingly.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863617584,
          "start": 1789863615573
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc2f5c550014qyhZ8GKq2mMr6",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc2f574d0013e7HsB54Bfmgf2",
      "session_id": "ses_f43d0a935ffeNKe2t6MY9tOejv",
      "time_created": 1789863615573,
      "time_updated": 1789863617585
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tb5bsj1jL9RGQlDM",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import firebase_admin\nfrom firebase_admin import credentials, auth\nimport os\n\ndef register_user(email, password):\n    if not firebase_admin._apps:\n        # Initialize Firebase Admin SDK if not already initialized\n        # Replace 'path/to/your/serviceAccountKey.json' with the actual path to your Firebase service account key\n        # or use an environment variable for security in production.\n        # For example: os.environ.get(\"FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH\")\n        cred = credentials.Certificate(os.environ.get(\"FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH\", \"path/to/your/serviceAccountKey.json\"))\n        firebase_admin.initialize_app(cred)\n\n    try:\n        user = auth.create_user(\n            email=email,\n            password=password\n        )\n        return {\"uid\": user.uid, \"email\": user.email}\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise Exception(f\"Failed to register user: {e}\")\n\n",
            "filePath": "register_user.py"
          },
